<title>USA: Exxon shuts two units at Calif. refinery.</title>
<headline>Exxon shuts two units at Calif. refinery.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp shut a 26,000 barrel per day (bpd) coking unit and 29,000 bpd hydrocracker for scheduled maintenance at its Benicia, Calif., refinery, according to a company spokesman.</p>
<p>The coker was taken down Feb 2 while the hydrocracker was shut Jan 31.</p>
<p>The company declined to say when the two units would be restarted.</p>
<p>The refinery, which has total crude distillation capacity of 128,000 bpd and catalytic cracking capacity of 69,000 bpd, lies east of San Francisco.</p>
<p>-- Matt Daily, New York Energy Desk 212-859-1626</p>
